      "id": "lpic2-smart-monitor-identity",
      "version": 1,
      "track": "LPIC-2",
      "unit": "linux-ata-smart-maintenance",
      "topic": "ATA storage diagnostics and monitoring",
      "title": "Keep the right disks under SMART monitoring after a rename",
      "summary": "Repair saved monitoring rules so they keep watching the intended disks when the Linux path names change.",
      "objective": "Watch health and the self-test log for the supplied primary disk in both layouts. Keep one health-only rule for the supplied auxiliary disk in both layouts. Save a readable configuration with just those intended devices and verify both previews.",
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "minutes": 15,
      "retry_guidance": "Use the failed requirement and the latest output or selected preview. Repair the specific mismatch and check again.",
      "steps": [
        "Understand the task",
        "Try the separate example",
        "Complete the independent assignment"
      ],
      "guide": [
        {
          "title": "Understand the task",
          "why": "The first field is a device name or path. In this SMART configuration subset, -H enables overall health monitoring and -l selftest asks to watch the self-test log. A # comment is ignored.",
          "action": "Read the worked example.",
          "commands": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Investigate with separate inputs",
          "why": "The same name, such as /dev/sda, can refer to a different disk after maintenance. The supplied /dev/disk/by-id/ paths follow the serials in both layouts. In the preview, compare which serial each rule would monitor.",
          "action": "Compare the guided practice output and supplied device facts.",
          "commands": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Complete the independent assignment",
          "why": "The current device identities and outcomes determine credit.",
          "action": "Check the independent task after making changes.",
          "commands": []
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The saved rules resolve to the intended primary and auxiliary disk in both represented layouts. The primary keeps health and self-test monitoring, and the auxiliary keeps its original health check.",
      "hints": [
        "Expand the supplied paths and compare the same serial across both layouts.",
        "Save the edited file before comparing previews. The flags follow the device on the same line.",
        "Check that all expected checks are on their own intended serial. A rule on a reused name can select the other disk even though the file parses."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/exam-201-202-objectives/",
        "https://github.com/smartmontools/smartmontools/blob/main/src/smartctl.8.in",
        "https://www.smartmontools.org/static/doxygen/smartd_8cpp_source.html",
        "https://github.com/mirror/smartmontools/blob/master/smartd.conf.5.in"
      ],
      "simplifications": "The supplied virtual ATA drives model disk identity, overall health, a bounded short test and its self-test log. The saved smartd.conf subset previews explicit device rules in two supplied layouts. No host device access, kernel or service changes, physical timings, extended tests, arbitrary shell, device scans, SSH, actual SMART commands, alerts or hardware monitoring.",
